{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:conditional-matching-separation",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "If \\(\\mathrm{oeq:global\\text{-}endpoint\\text{-}response}\\) is resolved affirmatively, there is a finite constant \\(C\\) such that, for all sufficiently large \\(n_\\ast\\),\n\\[\n \\rho_n^\\ast\\le C\\left(\\frac{\\log n_\\ast}{n_\\ast}\\right)^{s/(2s+d)}.\n\\]\nTogether with Theorem 6, this gives, for all sufficiently large \\(n_\\ast\\), the conditional matching frontier\n\\[\n c\\left(\\frac{\\log n_\\ast}{n_\\ast}\\right)^{s/(2s+d)}\n \\le\\rho_n^\\ast\\le\n C\\left(\\frac{\\log n_\\ast}{n_\\ast}\\right)^{s/(2s+d)}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "c",
      "C",
      "n_\\ast",
      "s",
      "d",
      "\\rho_n^\\ast"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "oeq:global-endpoint-response",
      "thm:uniform-margin-band",
      "thm:sharp-separation-lower",
      "def:testing-frontier"
    ],
    "justification": "This proposition isolates the only endpoint-response-dependent part of the minimax frontier from the unconditional lower theorem.",
    "gap": "Existing smooth optimal-transport estimation rates do not yield a global cross-Hessian margin test; the upper inequality follows only after the boundary-uniform endpoint response is established.",
    "consumer": "Analysts obtain the exact attainable order once the stated analytic endpoint question is settled, without weakening the unconditional impossibility result.",
    "proof_tex": "Assume that \\(\\mathrm{oeq:global\\text{-}endpoint\\text{-}response}\\) is resolved affirmatively.  Fix the confidence level \\(\\delta=0.05\\), which belongs to \\((0,1/4)\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{thm:uniform\\text{-}margin\\text{-}band}\\), for every sufficiently large \\(n_\\ast\\), the test \\(\\Psi_n\\) then satisfies\n\\[\n \\sup_{\\mathbf P\\in\\mathcal M_s:\\,\\gamma_{pq}\\le0}\n \\mathbb P_{\\mathbf P}(\\Psi_n=1)\\le0.05\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n \\sup_{\\mathbf P\\in\\mathcal M_s:\\,\\gamma_{pq}\\ge3w_n}\n \\mathbb P_{\\mathbf P}(\\Psi_n=0)\\le0.05<0.20.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\Psi_n\\) is feasible in the optimization defining \\(\\rho_n^\\ast\\) in \\(\\mathrm{def:testing\\text{-}frontier}\\) at separation \\(3w_n\\).  By the defining infimum,\n\\[\n \\rho_n^\\ast\\le3w_n\n =3\\left(\\frac2m+\\frac{2M}{m^2}\\right)C_1\n \\left\\{\\frac{\\log(C_0Rn_\\ast/0.05)}{n_\\ast}\\right\\}^{s/(2s+d)}.\n \\tag{1}\n\\]\nPut \\(A=C_0R/0.05>0\\).  For \\(n_\\ast\\ge\\max\\{2,A\\}\\),\n\\[\n \\log(An_\\ast)=\\log A+\\log n_\\ast\n \\le 2\\log n_\\ast.\n\\]\nBecause \\(s/(2s+d)>0\\), equation (1), with all fixed factors absorbed into a finite constant \\(C\\), gives\n\\[\n \\rho_n^\\ast\\le C\n \\left(\\frac{\\log n_\\ast}{n_\\ast}\\right)^{s/(2s+d)}\n\\]\nfor all sufficiently large \\(n_\\ast\\).  Under the strict-slack premise of \\(\\mathrm{thm:sharp\\text{-}separation\\text{-}lower}\\), that established theorem supplies a constant \\(c>0\\) and a threshold beyond which\n\\[\n \\rho_n^\\ast\\ge c\n \\left(\\frac{\\log n_\\ast}{n_\\ast}\\right)^{s/(2s+d)}.\n\\]\nTaking the maximum of the upper- and lower-bound thresholds proves the displayed conditional matching frontier.",
